# ROSCO files
*.85
*.i90
*local*
*build*

# TWO NEGATIONS, EACH FOR A FILE ONE OF THOSE TWO PATTERNS SWALLOWED, AND EACH
# FOUND ONLY BECAUSE SOMETHING ELSE BROKE. `git status` is clean the whole time
# a needed file is missing, which is what makes this shape expensive:
#
#   *build*  swallowed fixtures/bladed_stub/build.sh, so the first commit of the
#            oracle fixture added the .c and left the script that builds it
#            untracked -- a committed evidence file naming a library nothing
#            committed could produce (K3). Unit #5, second dispatch.
#   *local*  swallowed rosco/controller/src/vit_localvariables_view.f90, a
#            GENERATED view populator that CMakeLists compiles and the
#            ExtController wrapper USEs. A fresh clone would not build. Unit #5,
#            third dispatch.
#
# Negations rather than `git add -f`, so the NEXT generated file with `local` or
# `build` in its name is not swallowed too. After committing any new fixture or
# generated source, run `git check-ignore -v` on each file rather than trusting
# a clean status.
!rosco/controller/src/vit_*_view.f90
!fixtures/**/build.sh

# Binaries
*.dylib
*.so
*.dll.*
*.bts

