.vit_build_wrapper.sh
kgen_*/
# The KGen kernel fixture. An extraction leftover like the four lines around it
# -- `scripts/reset_to_clean.sh` has always removed it, and it has never been
# tracked -- but it was the only one not named here, so every unit that ran an
# extraction left `?? kernel/` behind and had to delete it by hand to satisfy
# done.py's clean-tree predicate. Unit #11's second dispatch could not (its
# session had no permission to remove a directory) and would have had to choose
# between an unclean tree and committing 62 state files plus object code.
# Anything inside worth keeping is COPIED to evidence/<Unit>/ by convention --
# the verify_fields.csv, the generated .f90, the statefile list.
kernel/
model/
elapsedtime/
kgen.log
.vit_wrapper.log
model.ini
.loop-run/
translations/*/*_test/

# ExtController oracle fixture: a BUILD PRODUCT of fixtures/bladed_stub/discon_stub.c.
# The .c is the artifact; the .so is rebuilt by fixtures/bladed_stub/build.sh.
fixtures/bladed_stub/*.so
# ...and the script that rebuilds it is NOT a build product. `*build*` above
# matches `build.sh`, so the first commit of this fixture silently left it
# untracked: an evidence file naming a library that nothing committed could
# produce (K3). Same shape as the gitignored `Examples/DISCON.IN` that let a
# crashed probe reconfigure the gate where no clean-tree check could see it --
# a pattern broad enough to catch a directory is broad enough to catch a file
# somebody needs.
!fixtures/bladed_stub/build.sh

# ADDED by unit #36 (PitchSaturation), 2026-08-14. `*build*` above is upstream
# ROSCO's, and it matches by FILENAME anywhere in the tree -- so an evidence
# artifact called `<something>build<something>.txt` is silently untracked. Five
# existed when this was found, across four units, and every one of them is the
# artifact that records a FAILURE:
#
#   evidence/CheckInputs/mutation.integrated-build-INVALID.json
#   evidence/NonDecreasing/loop_defects/build.error.txt
#   evidence/PIDController/vit_defects/callees_h_missing_types.build.txt
#   evidence/PIIController/postintegration_transient_build_failure.txt   <- STATUS.md tells its story in prose
#   evidence/PitchSaturation/vit_redtest_build_failure.txt
#
# `git add -A` reports nothing and the commit looks complete, which is K3's
# failure mode with no symptom. Narrow on purpose: object files and build logs
# under evidence/*/…/out/ stay ignored, because those are outputs and not
# records. Closing by addition rather than by editing line 65 (P5).
!evidence/**/*build*.txt
!evidence/**/*build*.json
!evidence/**/*build*.md
